From here on out, we don't
have a single second to spare.

53
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,505
Joestar's life is on the line.

54
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:33,580
Thank you.

55
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,060
Best of luck, Okuyasu.

56
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,360
Sing to you, Koichi.

57
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,997
In about 20 minutes, we'll finally
arrive at the Port of Morio, Mr.

58
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,910
Joestar.

59
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,140
Is that right?

60
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,440
I seem to have misplaced my cane.

61
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,780
Have you seen it?

62
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:18,432
Isn't that it right in front of you, sir?

63
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,900
So he's my father, huh?

64
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,130
Josuke?

65
00:04:33,213 --> 00:04:34,081
Are you alright?

66
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,700
I'm just processing.

67
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,937
I've never met this guy in my life.

68
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,785
Yet I'm supposed to accept
that he's my father.

69
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,180
I don't know, it's...

70
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:55,217
But the only thing that
matters right now is

71
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:57,657
his life is in danger
if I didn't even lift

72
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:00,857
a finger to help I'd
always regret it besides

73
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:03,411
my mom would fall apart if the guy croaked

74
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:11,540
Damn that Jotaro if he left you two mouth
breathers behind to sniff out my user

75
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:16,420
That means he completely saw through
my remote controlled playing trick

76
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,920
There you are chili pepper

77
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:28,600
I'll give this to Jotaro Kujo,
the man's sharp as a tack.

78
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:33,632
He's the last person I'd want finding me.

79
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,240
He'd just kill my five.

80
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,296
Speaking of killing,

81
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,857
this remote-controlled
Spitfire plane can reach

82
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,587
Joseph Joestar's boat
in a mere five minutes.

83
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:47,680
A dinged-up old motorboat, on the other
hand, would take about eight to ten.

84
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,030
Meaning,

85
00:05:49,113 --> 00:05:52,077
if I can put you two down for
a dirt nap in three minutes,

86
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:54,297
it'll give me time to
catch up and pass them.

87
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:57,237
Wait, are you trying to tell
me you're Silly Peppers, user?

88
00:05:57,320 --> 00:06:00,340
You're looking at Akira Otoishi, age 19.

89
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:03,309
Oh, and don't let the
guitar throw you off.

90
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:09,744
One day I want to be a rocking guitarist,
the likes of Jimi Hendrix and Jeff Beck.

91
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:13,497
That's why I keep this sweet little
mama on my person 24 hours a day,

92
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:14,639
seven days a week.

93
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:18,694
One day the masses will look
up from their mundane lives

94
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:23,591
And they'll be lining up for miles to
let my music knock them off their feet

95
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:31,600
People around the world
will know my name Oh yeah

96
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:38,175
This can't be good I never thought a
stand user would come out of hiding

97
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:41,037
Which means there's no
doubt in his mind that he

98
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:44,238
can slaughter both me and
Josuke without much trouble

99
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:51,326
I'm ready for round two with Shining
Diamond, but I'll only use my little pinky,

100
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,380
just like I did with Okuyasu.

101
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:55,467
You should get back, Koichi.

102
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:01,100
It's game on, Josuke Higashikata!

103
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,640
Just a minute. Huh?

104
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:06,017
If you're planning to use only
your pinky in this showdown,

105
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,977
then I've got a couple of rules of my own.

106
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,437
You can take your rules
and shove them, fool!

107
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,814
Rules are wasted on a pup kid like you!

108
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,550
Ah!

109
00:07:16,633 --> 00:07:17,640
You damn bastard!

110
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:19,040
How dare you!

111
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,837
Well, you did say that
rules are wasted on me.

112
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:25,197
You also said something about bringing
me down with your pinky finger.

113
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,460
So what's the wannabe
rocker Otoishi gonna do now?

114
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,240
I'll kill you!

115
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,694
You already said that!

116
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:34,035
Don't you have any new material, fool?

117
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,080
The pain in my finger is unbearable!

118
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:40,540
I have to redirect it onto something!

119
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:45,940
This gnawing rage, I
have defense to someone!

120
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,770
Awesome!

121
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:23,160
First I'll kill you, then the old gas bag!

122
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,860
After that, your precious mommies!

123
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,600
That was pure ecstasy.

124
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,280
My heart is free again.

125
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:36,522
There's no greater euphoria than
letting your blistering rage fly.

126
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,140
Let's test that theory, Otoishi!

127
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,580
What the hell?

128
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:45,757
How'd he...

129
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:50,420
I know Stans can move at incredible
speeds, but this is different.

130
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:53,545
It's like he found a way
to teleport behind me.

131
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,837
No, Josuke, that's not what happened.

132
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,273
I was able to see everything back there.

133
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,457
Otoishi didn't take a single step.

134
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,658
You're the one who changed position.

135
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:04,920
Something moved you. Say what?

136
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:07,437
Chili Peppers suddenly
appeared and flipped Shining

137
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:10,873
Diamond around 180 degrees
without you even realizing it.

138
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:14,140
Just look, you're facing the ocean.

139
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:16,280
Chili Pepper did that?

140
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,960
Where is he now, Koichi?

141
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,200
I don't see that sparky bastard.

142
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,897
He's hiding underground.

143
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:25,509
He's using the storm
drains to come and go.

144
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:29,337
He popped halfway out of the
drain to turn you around.

145
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:32,337
There must be underground electrical
lines running all over the place.

146
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:36,817
A little soul searching always gives
me the boost I need to bring the pain.

147
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:38,429
Behind you, on your right.

148
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,980
He's right behind you!

149
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:57,497
He bolts back into the electrical
wires at the last second,

150
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,797
and his speed makes him hard to pin down.

151
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,697
Jotaro's the only one
who can keep up with him.

152
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:02,857
What are we gonna do?

153
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,057
Here in the harbor,

154
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:07,677
you don't have the luxury of digging
up asphalt and severing all the wires.

155
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:09,720
Josuke Higashkata. However,

156
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:13,297
the bigger the opening you make
in the ground with shiny diamonds,

157
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:17,117
the easier it is to surface from
below and knock your lights out!

158
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,612
Josuke is on your right!

159
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:19,980
No, in front!

160
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,430
Behind you!

161
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,830
No, ladies!

162
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,697
This is like a game of
whack-a-mole on steroids!

163
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:32,427
I can't follow his movements at
all when he's going that fast!

164
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:35,917
What's the matter, Josuke?

165
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,020
Can't keep your eye on the birdie!

166
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,410
Josuke, no!

167
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:43,140
Well, look at that.

168
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,555
Two minutes to spare.

169
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:47,288
That gives me plenty
of time to finish this.

170
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:54,237
Hey, Koichi, keep track of Chili
Pepper's location and call it out to me.

171
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:57,880
At this range, he's moving too
fast for my eyes to follow.

172
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:00,337
But if you can't follow
him, how am I supposed to?

173
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:02,397
As soon as I find him, he disappears.

174
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,656
Then you have to look harder, Koichi.

175
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:08,879
We're about to win this and by now
you should know what I'm thinking.

176
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,460
I should?

177
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:17,315
That muck on the ground, the
asphalt's turned into tar.

178
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:21,515
And the drains are covered
in all the oil from the tar.

179
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,840
I get it now.

180
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:27,537
When Josuke struck the ground, he reduced
the asphalt to its most basic ingredients.

181
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,580
Which means...

182
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,413
Behind you on the left!

183
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,140
Oh, yeah.

184
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:38,556
Right in the kisser!

185
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:40,758
Well, that's great.

186
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:42,901
Our strategy worked like a charm.

187
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:47,778
Yes, I'm the superstar now, because
I'm gonna rock this loser's world.

188
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:58,710
Huh?

189
00:11:58,793 --> 00:11:59,623
It's the boat!

190
00:11:59,706 --> 00:12:00,971
He's dead ahead, Jochiro!

191
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:02,920
See? We're almost there!

192
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,629
Don't drop your cards yet.

193
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:06,230
Whoa!

194
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:08,516
What the hell's happening over there?

195
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:10,280
Josuke! Koichi!

196
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,099
What's that light?

197
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:17,180
I underestimated you, Josuke Higashikata.

198
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:21,377
I was too focused on my presentation and
should have just gone in for the kill.

199
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,048
But I've learned my lesson.

200
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,000
The juvenile me is no more.

201
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,260
I'm reborn as a killing machine!

202
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:30,400
And for my first act of anarchy,

203
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:33,557
I'll focus all of Morio's
electricity into Jelly Pepper!

204
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,000
This is my last resort!

205
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:39,137
Using this technique means temporarily
knocking out power all over town,

206
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:42,080
which I'm forced to draw
on for my lifeblood!

207
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,580
But none of that matters now!

208
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:49,197
After I've done away with you cretins,
I'll bolt over to the RC plane's battery,

209
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,162
then I'll lie over to
Joseph and slit his throat!

210
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:54,450
What the?

211
00:12:54,533 --> 00:12:55,720
I can't see a thing!

212
00:12:58,340 --> 00:12:59,170
Bastards!

213
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:13,760
I don't believe it!

214
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:16,138
Chili Pepper got the best of Josuke!

215
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,510
Josuke!

216
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:26,540
Is it sinking in yet?

217
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:30,020
This entire town's electrical
power is at my disposal.

218
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:32,897
And to really drive the point home,

219
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:37,098
I'll be sure to charge my electric
bill for the month to your address.

220
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:41,020
It slides out, Josuke!

221
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:46,280
Is that a tire?

222
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:53,040
Just as I expected, you were
too dense to figure it out.

223
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:55,770
Huh?

224
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,440
Now I understand!

225
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,337
You blew up that tire on purpose!

226
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:02,117
It was all part of your plan
to entomb my stand in rubber!

227
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,030
Of course!

228
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:06,457
Rubber is an insulator so it
doesn't conduct electricity!

229
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,599
Chili Pepper is powerless in there!

230
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:09,640
Damn it all!

231
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,190
All right!

232
00:14:11,273 --> 00:14:12,977
We just have to wait for Jojaro now!

233
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:13,890
Just kidding!

234
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:18,520
A good idea, but that's
not gonna work on me! Ha!

235
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:21,857
Your plan might have succeeded
had the rubber been a meter thick!

236
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:25,257
But this flimsy excuse for a trap
doesn't even register as a threat!

237
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:27,399
So let me show you some real power!

238
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:28,570
Dumbass!

239
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:34,280
You lost this battle, Josuke!

240
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:37,640
Just great.

241
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,117
You really are as stupid as you look.

242
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:44,097
Having your stand break through the tire
was the dumbest thing you could have done.

243
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:45,010
Huh?

244
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:47,410
Huh?

245
00:14:47,493 --> 00:14:49,680
I forgot about the air in the tire!

246
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,684
The pressure release
launched him like a rocket!

247
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:57,510
No!

248
00:14:57,593 --> 00:14:58,423
Not the ocean!

249
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,320
Anything but the ocean!

250
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,797
Oh, yeah, that's right.

251
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:04,762
Salt water conducts electricity.

252
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:08,937
And in the ocean, the electricity that
